 "intro": "School and university words, with several false friends of English.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "carrera",
   "significado": "university degree course",
   "pron": "ka-RRE-ra",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Here it means university studies, not a competition. «Estudio la carrera de Medicina» is very normal.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "asignatura",
   "significado": "school or university subject",
   "pron": "a-sig-na-TU-ra",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Do not say «sujeto»: a school subject is an «asignatura». «Sujeto» is the subject of a sentence.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "aprobar",
   "significado": "to pass",
   "pron": "a-pro-BAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The o becomes ue: «apruebo», «aprueba», but «aprobamos». Its opposite is «suspender».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "suspender",
   "significado": "to fail",
   "pron": "sus-pen-DER",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "With an exam it is not «to suspend»: it means to fail. The bad mark is called «suspenso».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "nota",
   "significado": "mark; grade",
   "pron": "NO-ta",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The verb for getting a mark is «sacar»: «saco un ocho». In Spain marks go from 0 to 10, and a five is a pass.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "beca",
   "significado": "scholarship; grant",
   "pron": "BE-ka",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You ask for a beca with «pedir» or get one with «conseguir». A «beca de estudios» helps to pay for university.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "matricularse",
   "significado": "to enrol; to register",
   "pron": "ma-tri-ku-LAR-se",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It goes with «en»: «me matriculo en Historia». It is a verb with «se», like «levantarse».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "instituto",
   "significado": "secondary school",
   "pron": "ins-ti-TU-to",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "In Spain, after primary school you go to the «instituto». There you do the ESO and, if you want, the bachillerato.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "máster",
   "significado": "master's degree",
   "pron": "MAS-ter",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It has an accent: MÁS-ter. The plural is «másteres». It is usually done after the degree.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "apuntes",
   "significado": "class notes",
   "pron": "a-PUN-tes",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is almost always plural: «tomar apuntes» in class and «repasar los apuntes» at home.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "repasar",
   "significado": "to revise; to review",
   "pron": "rre-pa-SAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It starts with «re-», which means «again»: you study again what you already saw.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
