   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The school system and its false friends",
     "texto": [
      "In Spain you study at **el colegio** (primary school) and then at **el instituto**: the ESO runs from age 12 to 16 and the **bachillerato**, optional, from 16 to 18. At university you do **un grado** and then you can go on with **un máster** or **un doctorado**.\n\nMarks go from 0 to 10: below 5 is **suspenso**; **aprobado** is 5 to 6.9; **notable**, 7 to 8.9; and **sobresaliente**, 9 to 10.\n\nWatch out for false friends:\n\n- **carrera** means university studies (and also a sports race).\n- **colegio** is a school, not a «college».\n- **asignatura** is a school subject; **sujeto** is the subject of a sentence.\n- **suspender** an exam means to fail it."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Si + present and cuando + subjunctive",
     "texto": [
      "To talk about the future with conditions, two formulas are very useful:\n\n- **Si** + present → future: **Si estudias, aprobarás**. It is a possible condition.\n- **Cuando** + subjunctive → future: **Cuando termine la carrera, haré un máster**. If the moment has not arrived yet, the verb after «cuando» is subjunctive.\n\nWith habits, «cuando» takes the ordinary present: **Cuando estudio, apago el móvil**.\n\nFor what has just happened use the present perfect (**he** + participle): **He suspendido Estadística**. The participle of **aprobar** is **aprobado** and of **sacar**, **sacado**."
     ],
